          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறியாமை — aṟiyāmai — \"ignorance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அவன் அறியாமையால் அந்தத் தவறைச் செய்தான். avaṉ aṟiyāmaiyāl antat tavaṟaic ceytāṉ. He made that mistake out of ignorance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறி, to know + -ஆ-, not + -மை: not-knowing. பொறாமை, envy, has the same shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறியாமை (aṟiyāmai) is native: aṟi, \"to know\" (DEDR 314), with the negative -ஆ- and the abstract ending -மை: \"the state of not knowing\"."
            }
          ]
        },
